e2defrag (0.79) unstable; urgency=low

  * Fixed inode sort order so lower inodes move left
  * Add -F and -D switches to specify default file and directory
    priorities
  * Change block group forcing ( not first trying to allocate from
    the inode's native group ) to take place at priority > 50 instead
    of > 0, and added ability to force to the right for priorities
    < -50.
  * Various optimizations
  * Removed dependency on glib
  * Improved the progress indicator to show percent completion
  * Removed -b bad-block-inode option
  * Cleaned up the man page
  * Auto detect buffer pool size based on free memory
  * Repackaged to update to source format 3.0 (native)

 -- Phillip Susi <psusi@ubuntu.com>  Thu, 21 Jun 2012 13:56:09 -0400

