 -- Phillip Susi <psusi@cfl.rr.com>  Thu, 10 Jun 2010 21:30:46 -0400

defrag (0.76) lucid; urgency=low

  * Added support for ext4 extents
  * Optimizations: Use O_DIRECT io and readv/writev to batch
    requests and avoid polluting the buffer cache and wasting
    cpu time copying to/from it.  Also increased the buffer
    hash table size which saved a good bit of cpu time.
  * Fixed priority polarity: Positive priority means move
    blocks to the left, negative means to the right.
  * Fixed force behavior.  We were forcing one block at a time
    in reverse order and not updating the display to show the
    forces.  The reverse order was causing horrid performance.
  * New extent based block map code.  The old double array system
    needed 600 mb of ram just for the relocation maps on a 320 gb
    drive.  It is now possible to defrag a Terrabyte+ fs without
    dozens of gb of ram.

 -- Phillip Susi <psusi@cfl.rr.com>  Mon, 31 May 2010 11:48:39 -0400

defrag (0.75) lucid; urgency=low

  * Added support for flex_bg and csum features
  * Corrected display to show blocks being read from as
    "R" instead of the blocks they will be written to
  * Fixed "musical blocks" bug where block positions would
    change on repeated invocations rather than being deterministic
  * Changed block allocator to force blocks to the left instead
    of allocating from their native block group when they have
    been given a negative priority in the priority file

 -- Phillip Susi <psusi@cfl.rr.com>  Sun, 11 Apr 2010 17:06:46 -0400

