defrag (0.73pjm1-1) unstable; urgency=low

  * New upstream release, by Peter J. Moulder <pjm@bofh.asn.au>:
    o Builds with current libc6-dev.
    o Support >1k block sizes (closes: #48458, #62556).
    o Support sparse_super and ext2 compression.
    o Reject ext2 filesystems that have unsupported features.
    o Uses autoconf.
    o Installs into /usr/sbin instead of /sbin.  (This is more conformant
      with FHS.)
    o Minix defrag now called mdefrag.
    o Manpage symlinks created.
    o (hopefully this release will be numbered 0.74 after contact with
      Stephen Tweedie ...)
  * Lots of packaging changes thanks to Peter as well:
    o debian/rules:
      support for DEB_BUILD_OPTIONS (including noopt to disable -O2)
    o debian/control: Build-Depends: debhelper (>= 2.0.40)
      Standards-Version 3.5.2
    o debian/dirs: No longer required, removed ...
    o debian/docs: INSTALL file removed from package
  * debian/control:
    o Architecture: i386 just to be safe for the moment
    o fixed typo in Build-Depends: dephelper -> debhelper (closes: #102009)
    o Build-Depends: bzip2 for test suite ...
  * Fixed reference to '/etc/frag' from frag(8), this now refers
    to /sbin/frag (closes: #66834, #66835)
  * These llseek bugs *should* be fixed ... (closes: #19998, #44025, #60868)

 -- Timshel Knoll <timshel@debian.org>  Thu,  5 Jul 2001 00:15:04 +1000

defrag (0.73-2) unstable; urgency=low

  * Packaging taken over by Timshel Knoll <timshel@debian.org>
  * Re-packaged from scratch. Found pristine sources on web and built
    with .orig.tar.gz & .diff.gz (0.73-1 was just a .tar.gz)
    (closes: Bug#44165)
  * Merged in Adam Heath's changes one by one, with a brief comment for
    each one.
  * Policy 3.1.1 (added Build-Depends:) 
  * Priority: optional (doesn't need to be `extra')
  * Removed edefrag and xdefrag from the package: the extended and xia
    filesystems are no longer supported by the kernel.
  * Incorporated Paul Slootman's alpha diffs (closes: Bug#22209)
  * Undocumented binary e2dump - filed bug and symlinked.

